===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To put (land, property) in escheat; to [[confiscate]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=w:Peter H. Wilson|title=The Holy Roman Empire|page=329|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2017
|passage=Failure to perform duties opened the culprit to charges of ‘felony’ (''felonia''), providing grounds for the king to '''escheat''' the fief.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To revert to a [[state]] or [[lord]] because its previous owner died without an heir.

